{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"IncidentHyperedgeIndices"},{"kind":"text","text":" = "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/IncidenceMatrix","preciseIdentifier":"s:21IncidenceMatrixModule0aB0V","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"IncidenceMatrix"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/IncidenceMatrix\/MemberIndices","preciseIdentifier":"s:21IncidenceMatrixModule0aB0V13MemberIndicesV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MemberIndices"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix"]]},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix\/IncidentHyperedgeIndices"},"sections":[],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"IncidentHyperedgeIndices","kind":"identifier"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix.swift#L203"},"externalID":"s:21IncidenceMatrixModule08OrientedaB0V24IncidentHyperedgeIndicesa","roleHeading":"Type Alias","symbolKind":"typealias","title":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix.IncidentHyperedgeIndices","modules":[{"name":"IncidenceMatrixModule"}],"extendedModule":"IncidenceMatrixModule","fragments":[{"text":"typealias","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"IncidentHyperedgeIndices","kind":"identifier"}]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/orientedincidencematrix\/incidenthyperedgeindices"]}],"abstract":[{"text":"The stored row of either plane, read in place.","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule":{"abstract":[],"type":"topic","title":"IncidenceMatrixModule","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule","url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule","role":"collection"},"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule/OrientedIncidenceMatrix/IncidentHyperedgeIndices":{"title":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix.IncidentHyperedgeIndices","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"IncidentHyperedgeIndices"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix\/IncidentHyperedgeIndices","url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/orientedincidencematrix\/incidenthyperedgeindices","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The stored row of either plane, read in place.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"IncidentHyperedgeIndices"}]},"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule/OrientedIncidenceMatrix":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The oriented incidence matrix of a directed hypergraph: entry (v, p) is −1 when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"type":"text","text":" is a source"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of column "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"p"},{"type":"text","text":", +1 when it is a target, and 0 otherwise. Gallo, Longo, Pallottino and Nguyen"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(1993) define a directed hypergraph’s matrix this way (aᵢⱼ = −1 for a tail node, 1 for a head"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"node); a directed graph’s edge is the column with one source and one target, the matrix of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"spectral graph theory (B·Bᵀ = L, Godsil–Royle §8.3) and NetworkX’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidence_matrix(oriented=True)"},{"type":"text","text":". It conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedHypergraph"},{"type":"text","text":", so the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hypergraphs"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"algorithms (B- and F-connection, components, the clique expansion) run on it unchanged; it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/orientedincidencematrix","identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix","type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule/IncidenceMatrix/MemberIndices":{"title":"IncidenceMatrix.MemberIndices","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MemberIndices"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/IncidenceMatrix\/MemberIndices","url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/incidencematrix\/memberindices","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The indices of the set bits of one stored row, ascending, read in place: a column’s member"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"indices, or a vertex’s column indices ("},{"code":"IncidentHyperedgeIndices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"). No copy and no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"allocation, unlike a "},{"code":"BitSet","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". It shares the matrix’s words copy-on-write, so a later"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"mutation of the matrix leaves it unchanged."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MemberIndices"}]},"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule/IncidenceMatrix":{"abstract":[{"text":"The unoriented incidence matrix of a hypergraph: an n × m matrix of bits with cell (v, p) set","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"when vertex ","type":"text"},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a member of column ","type":"text"},{"code":"p","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". The vertices are "},{"code":"0..<vertexCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and the columns,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the hyperedges, are at positions "},{"code":"0..<hyperedgeCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". It conforms to "},{"code":"Hypergraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"Hypergraphs","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" algorithms run on it unchanged; it is not a "},{"code":"Graph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" even when built from one,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"because a cell edit can give a column any number of bits."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"IncidenceMatrix","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/IncidenceMatrix","url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/incidencematrix","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"IncidenceMatrix","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"IncidenceMatrix","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol"}}}